 "text": "Hey, how are you doing? Not at all. It' kinder than showing up at the reception and finding you can't stay due to a quick bite of cake. Say yes, and ask the bride to keep the space clear of nuts. Lots of couples do keep the room nut free for guests with allergies. No worries. Ask if they keep the room nut free and ask to sit near the door so you can leave immediately if you start to react. Weddings are supposed to be joyful, not stressful. If you really can't go, it' kinder to let them know before you go. Bring a small snack that doesn't contain nuts, just in case. It' always nice to share a cup of coffee with someone. You don't have to be. Just tell them upfront and take a gentle approach. Most people do keep the nut free room, and you'll be the hero for going.",
